Deltas are NOT composable. Two causes, and only the first is a measurement
artifact: (1) logit-scale drift, removed by --calibrate; (2) sign() is
idempotent-ish, so binarising an input that an upstream binarised layer has
already coarsened costs less than binarising a full-precision one. (2) is a
real property of the architecture and means single-component deltas are an
UPPER BOUND on their marginal cost inside a fully binary model.

